      },
      {
        "block_id": "ZDvgdE5EAo23ODxjc8IcxdeInlh",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Modern AI applications, especially in the Internet of Things (IoT) and autonomous driving, typically reason over rich, structured events: a sensor reading with its timestamp and vector embedding, a diagnostic log with an error code and audio snippet, or a trip segment with location, speed, and scene context. These require the database to natively support the ingestion and search of nested data. ",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "SmjWd1TN4oZhOJxk0X6cr0Abnpd",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Instead of asking the user to convert their atomic structural events into flat data models, <include target=\"milvus\">Milvus</include><include target=\"zilliz\">Zilliz Cloud</include> introduces the Array of Structs, where each Struct in the array can hold scalars and vectors, preserving semantic integrity.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "WAV3dWE1PowuDGxcuMxcXNBOn60",
        "block_type": 4,
        "heading2": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Why Array of Structs",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "Bv9tdtz5GoaJPmxAmP8cwMoTngd",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Modern AI applications, from autonomous driving to multimodal retrieval, increasingly rely on nested, heterogeneous data. Traditional flat data models struggle to represent complex relationships like \"",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "one document with many annotated chunks",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "\" or \"",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "one driving scene with multiple observed maneuvers",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "\". This is where the Array of Structs data type in <include target=\"milvus\">Milvus</include><include target=\"zilliz\">Zilliz Cloud</include> shines.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "GLASdWqGKouDxxx5FDvct895nee",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "An Array of Structs allows you to store an ordered set of structured elements, where each Struct contains its own combination of scalar fields and vector embeddings. This makes it ideal for:",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "LD70dmM81oW24GxbGgBcAbXXnIc",
        "block_type": 12,
        "bullet": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Hierarchical data",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ": Parent entities with multiple child records, such as a book with many text chunks, or a video with many annotated frames.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "AWigd4gn1ognjVx0GjNcF7Cfn1f",
        "block_type": 12,
        "bullet": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Multimodal embeddings",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ": Each Struct can hold multiple vectors, such as text embedding plus image embedding, alongside metadata.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "Ekoxd7qyNosSyAxcCWDcPgQfnmg",
        "block_type": 12,
        "bullet": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Temporal or sequential data",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": true,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": ": Structs in an Array field naturally represent time-series or step-by-step events.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        },
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "PAiyd0TxzoYP3Cx4TqrcIcZQnWf",
        "block_type": 2,
        "parent_id": "EmRZdpJ1No87NhxLKT1cDFxqnHR",
        "text": {
          "elements": [
            {
              "text_run": {
                "content": "Unlike traditional workarounds that store JSON blobs or split data across multiple collections, the Array of Structs provides native schema enforcement, vector indexing, and efficient storage within <include target=\"milvus\">Milvus</include><include target=\"zilliz\">Zilliz Cloud</include>.",
                "text_element_style": {
                  "bold": false,
                  "inline_code": false,
                  "italic": false,
                  "strikethrough": false,
                  "underline": false
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "align": 1,
            "folded": false
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "block_id": "Ws3rdRkduoAtYpxeTsQclQumnSc",
